-- title:
--   Rational endomorphism subring acts on the projective Weierstrass model
-- statement:
--   Let $k$ be an algebraically closed field and $X$ a Weierstrass curve over $k$ which is elliptic, and write $E \to \operatorname{Spec} k$ for the structure morphism `projModelStrCR X.toProjective` of the projective Weierstrass model, so that for $t : T \to \operatorname{Spec} k$ the $T$-points are the pairs consisting of a morphism $T \to E$ whose composite with the structure morphism is $t$. Assume given: a relative group law $G$ on $E$ over $k$, i.e. multiplication, unit and inverse operations on the $T$-points for every $k$-scheme $T$, satisfying the group axioms and compatible with base change along morphisms over $\operatorname{Spec} k$; a bijection $\mathrm{ev}$ from the points over the identity base $\operatorname{Spec}$ of $k \to k$ to the affine points of $X$ base changed to $k$; the hypothesis that $\mathrm{ev}$ carries $G.\mathrm{mul}$ to addition of points; and the hypothesis that whenever such a point $P$ factors as $\operatorname{Spec}$ of a ring homomorphism $\chi$ from the $Z$-chart ring of the model followed by the chart immersion `zChartι`, the pair $(\chi(\mathtt{xOverZ}), \chi(\mathtt{yOverZ}))$ is nonsingular and $\mathrm{ev}\,P$ is the corresponding affine point. Then there exists a map $\Phi$ from the carrier of [`WeierstrassCurve.rationalEndSubring k X`](def/WeierstrassCurve_RationalEnd.html#L32) — the subring of additive endomorphisms of the points of $X$ over $k$ generated by the rationally represented homomorphisms — to the endomorphisms of $E$ over $\operatorname{Spec} k$ such that: $\mathrm{ev}(\Phi(\alpha) \circ P) = \alpha(\mathrm{ev}\,P)$ for all such $P$; each $\Phi(\alpha)$ is a homomorphism for $G$ on $T$-points, $\Phi(\alpha) \circ G.\mathrm{mul}(P,Q) = G.\mathrm{mul}(\Phi(\alpha)\circ P, \Phi(\alpha) \circ Q)$ for every $t : T \to \operatorname{Spec} k$; $\Phi(1)$ is the identity endomorphism; $\Phi(\alpha\beta) = \Phi(\alpha) \circ \Phi(\beta)$ (written in diagrammatic order as $\Phi(\beta)$ followed by $\Phi(\alpha)$); and $\Phi(\alpha+\beta) \circ P = G.\mathrm{mul}(\Phi(\alpha) \circ P, \Phi(\beta) \circ P)$ for all $T$-points $P$.
--
--   This is the statement that the endomorphism ring of an elliptic curve over an algebraically closed field, defined through its action on points, is realised by genuine endomorphisms of the projective Weierstrass model which respect the relative group law functorially in the base, the assignment being unital, multiplicative up to reversal of order, and additive for the group law. It is used in the construction of relative group laws with quaternionic multiplication in the Čerednik–Drinfeld part of the development.
-- source:
